 "id": "s1f_shakeout_offer_quote_1p41x",
 "pattern": "\\$0\\.00612/ns|1\\.41× basis|1\\.41x basis",
 "current": "$0.00644/ns · 1.48× basis on 46000463 — the BILLED rate (bid + the real 80 GB disk line), read off the live instance record",
 "retired_by": "The $0.00612/ns · 1.41× figure was computed from the launcher's `dph≈` line, which is the OFFER's dph_total — the market FLOOR plus the disk line the search priced at 8 GB — not what the instance is billed (our BID plus the disk line for the 80 GB actually allocated). Measured $0 read-only 2026-07-27 (`vast_rate_forensics.py --probe`, run 30265697399): on instance 46000463 the offer quoted $0.17922/hr and the instance is billed $0.20272/hr, a $0.0235/hr gap that decomposes exactly into $0.0035 floor→bid plus $0.0200 of disk line, a 10.0× under-quote of storage. An offer-quote multiple is therefore a LOWER BOUND and `inflight_usd_per_ns.row()` now marks it as one. This is also what made the same host look like it rose from 1.41× to 1.82× — STRATEGY.md Appendix A 36."
},
